    "notes": "1. 'Cash and cash equivalents' is composed of the two line items explicitly detailed in Note 32. 'Term deposits and highly liquid investments (within three months)' are considered cash equivalents. The 'Term deposits' line on the main balance sheet includes both current and non-current portions; only the portion classified as cash equivalents (within three months) is included here. The non-current term deposits are not considered cash equivalents.\n2. 'Marketable securities' are defined as liquid, unrestricted investments intended to be sold in the near term (< 3 months). This maps to the current portion of 'Financial assets at fair value through profit or loss' and 'Financial assets at fair value through other comprehensive income'. For 2023, the FVOCI current asset was '–' (zero), so it is omitted.\n3. 'Total accounts receivable' is taken directly from the balance sheet line.\n4. 'Total current liabilities' is the sum of all items listed under the 'Current liabilities' section of the balance sheet.\n5. 'Total debt short term and long term' includes all borrowings and notes payable, split between current and non-current portions as presented on the balance sheet. This matches the definition used in the supplementary 'Capital Risk Management' table (Note 4.2).\n6. 'Total equity' and 'Total assets' are taken directly from the balance sheet totals.\n7. Scale is 1,000,000 (millions) as indicated by '(RMB in Millions)' in the statement header.\n8. Currency is Chinese Yuan (CNY), represented as RMB in the statement.",
